10:### Modules
12:* `ps2xAnalyzer`: scans ELF/functions and writes TOML config (`stubs`, `skip`, instruction patches).
13:* `ps2xRecomp`: reads TOML + ELF, decodes R5900 instructions, and generates C++ output.
14:* `ps2xRuntime`: hosts memory, function registration, syscall dispatch, and hardware stubs.
17:### Features
21:* Single-file or multi-file output.
22:* Configurable stubs, skips, and instruction patches.
25:### How It Works
28:* Parsing a PS2 ELF file to extract functions, symbols, and relocations
35:### Current Behavior
37:* `stubs` entries generate wrappers that call known runtime syscall/stub handlers by name.
38:* `stubs` also supports address bindings with `handler@0xADDRESS` for stripped games (for example `sceCdRead@0x00123456`).
43:* `skip` entries are not recompiled and generate explicit `ps2_stubs::TODO_NAMED(...)` wrappers.
