132:* Basic GS/VU/file/system stubs.
138:### Game Override Hooks
142:A game override is C++ code that runs during `loadELF` and can replace EE function bindings by address for one specific game build. IOP RPC/DMA behavior is handled by the `ps2xIOP` emulator and its runtime transport. This is separate from recompilation output and separate from global runtime stubs/syscalls.
147:* Register macro: `PS2_REGISTER_GAME_OVERRIDE(name, elfName, entry, crc32, applyFn)`
155:#### Recommended Iteration Loop
157:1. Run with minimal config and no aggressive skipping.
158:2. Fix hard blockers first (`function not found`, syscall TODO, critical IO stubs).
159:3. Use temporary return stubs only to classify call importance.
164:### Describing Your Game Project
166:A game project built with PS2Recomp can describe itself in a `.recomp.json` file at the root of its repository. Lists of recomp and decomp projects, such as [recomp.board](https://recomp.fyi), read that file instead of guessing the game, system and status from the README.
191:### Limitations
194:* Hardware emulation is partial and many paths are stubbed.
